            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Big Bank earnings show 'no weakness' so far, analyst says",
            "description": "<p>The third quarter earnings cycle is underway after Big Banks JPMorgan Chase (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPM\">JPM</a>), Goldman Sachs (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GS\">GS</a>), Wells Fargo (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WFC\">WFC</a>), and Citi (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/C\">C</a>) reported their results on Tuesday.</p>\n<p>Argus Research director of financial services research Stephen Biggar joins Market Catalysts to take a closer look at the sector as earnings kick off.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
